===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first task''', play normally until you find {{CI|Twisted Rudie|name=true}}, get in his sight, then try to find him again in another [[Floor]].
*'''For the second task''', try to join good runs to get far. If you are really good, you could join a Discord run, because upon completing [[Floor]] 60, you will complete the task. Alternatively, you could just keep doing runs and restart after Floor 5 until you complete the quest.
*'''For the third task''', you could just use {{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} and/or {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}} and keep spamming your ability while getting chased.
To complete all tasks in tandem, keep playing until Floor 11, hoping you get a Twisted Rudie. Also, use your Ability as much as possible.

==Strategies==
Rudie is pretty well-rounded due to his fully 3 {{Star}} [[Stats]], being able to extract quite well and having high potential when it comes to mobility.

Rudie's Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Rudie|name=true}}, allows him to dash forward by increasing both his [[Movement Speed]] by 50 units, giving him 65 Walk Speed and 75 Run Speed. You can utilize this to get around or avoid danger, like for example, when you end up getting cornered in some way, using his Ability can help you get out of the area unscathed. His cooldown is also very short, meaning it's easy to get around places and escape situations at almost any time, especially with [[Trinkets]] like {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}}. In [[Panic Mode]], you can dash into the [[Elevator]] making it easier to avoid dying to the Panic Mode timer and the [[Twisteds]] who get faster during that period.

Rudie's Ability gives him the ability to perhaps be a decent distractor if one has the skill to do so. Given its short cooldown and powerful speed boost, as well as his average Movement Speed and Stamina, things like the usual Distractor Trinkets like {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}} alongside cooldown reducing Trinkets and [[Cards]] are recommended. It should be noted that, even with Dog Plush, Rudie is only able to out-walk {{CI|Twisted Shrimpo|name=true}} at best, so a better option for Distracting would be {{CI|Flutter|name=true}} due to her similar Ability and better mobility Stats. You can also simply divert Twisteds away from teammates, or bring Twisteds to distractors, using your Ability to facilitate escape or passing.

{{TI|Peppermint Icing|name=true}} is a really good choice to use with him. The short cooldown makes it so gaining Stamina would be a lot faster, and seeing as how the Ability would be used in traversal/escaping, a time where Stamina would be appreciated, the added Stamina can help prolong sprinting and make the situations easier. You can also sprint on [[Treadmill Machines]] and periodically stop extracting to use his Ability, regenerating the 30 Stamina and allowing for more sprinting, thus faster extraction of Treadmill Machines.

Overall, Rudie is a great all-rounder, with incredible mobility and survivability. He's decent at extracting and has a potential to distract. He's a fairly good Toon in solo runs, especially due to his Ability.

